=== Symbolic c-map as a map of pairs (q, x, y) -> (Q, X, Y) ===

Given: y^2 = x*(x+1)*(x+q^2).
c-value: c = 2*q*y/(q^2 - x^2).
Target curve E_PCP(c): Y^2 = X*(X+1)*(X+c^2).

Question: is there a polynomial/rational map (q, x, y) -> (Q, X, Y) with Q=c?

E1 model change: [2/21, -40/63, 1/21, 0]
G1 on E_PCP(20/21): [-45/49, 10/343]
c1 = 48/55 (canonical |c| <= 1: 48/55)
